.TH MACHO\-MAPLITERAL 1 "October 2, 2026" "MachO-Tools 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
macho\-mapliteral \- map a byte literal to addresses, then find pointers to them
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macho\-mapliteral
.I literal
.RI [ binary | bundle ]
.RI [ file-offset ...]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-b | \-\-binary
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds each occurrence of a byte literal, maps the occurrence's file offset to
the virtual address the loader will place it at, and then searches the file for
pointers to that address.
.PP
This is the step that turns a format magic into the code that handles it: the
literal is the format, the pointer table beside it is the dispatch, and the
address the literal maps to is what those pointers refer to.
.PP
The literal search is per slice and the pointer search is whole\-file, so a
pointer may be reported in a slice other than the one whose literal was mapped.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-binary " " \fIpath\fR
The binary to read.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Write one JSON object to standard output and send prose to standard error.
Addresses are rendered as
.B "0x..."
strings rather than numbers.
.TP
.I file-offset
One or more absolute file offsets to map instead of searching for the literal.
Use this for a magic that is assembled at runtime and therefore never appears
whole in the file. Offsets are absolute, as reported by
.BR macho\-findliteral (1).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MACHO_BINARY
The binary to read when none is given on the command line.
.TP
.B MACHO_APP
An application bundle to read, tried after
.BR MACHO_BINARY .
.TP
.B MACHO_CONFIG
Path to a replacement
.IR config.json .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The literal was located and mapped.
.TP
.B 1
The tool ran and the literal was not present.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, including a non\-numeric file offset.
.TP
.B 3
The file could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
macho\-mapliteral LZ4 "/Applications/Some App.app"
macho\-mapliteral \\x1f\\x8b \-\-json /usr/bin/ssh | jq '.data.locations[].pointers'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Mapping offsets you already have:
.PP
.RS
.nf
macho\-mapliteral irrelevant 0x3f8a0 /usr/bin/ssh
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR macho\-findliteral (1),
.BR macho\-findcall (1),
.BR macho\-symlookup (1)